        {[
          { q: "What does Canvas UGC mean?", a: "Canvas UGC is a content delivery model where creators produce short-form videos and post them on brand-owned social accounts. The brand's account is the 'canvas' — creators make the content, but it lives on the brand's property. Creators are paid based on the views their content generates, typically at a CPM of $2-$6." },
          { q: "Is Canvas UGC the same as regular UGC?", a: "No. The content style is similar — authentic, creator-made video — but the delivery model is completely different. Traditional UGC creators deliver raw video files to a brand. Canvas UGC creators post directly on the brand's social accounts. This means the brand gets organic reach, audience data, and algorithmic signal that traditional UGC does not provide." },
          { q: "Do I need followers to do Canvas UGC?", a: "No. Canvas UGC creators post on brand accounts, not their own. Your follower count is irrelevant — what matters is your ability to create content that generates views. This makes Canvas UGC one of the most accessible entry points for new creators." },
          { q: "How much can I earn from Canvas UGC?", a: "With CPM rates of $2-$6, active Canvas UGC creators working across multiple brand programs earn $3K-$15K+ per month. Earnings depend on the number of programs you work with, the volume of content you produce, and how well your content performs organically." },
          { q: "Is Canvas UGC related to Canva?", a: "No. Despite the similar spelling, Canvas UGC has nothing to do with the Canva design platform. 'Canvas' in this context refers to the brand's social account being the blank canvas where creator content is posted." },
          { q: "What platforms support Canvas UGC?", a: "Primarily TikTok, Instagram Reels, YouTube Shorts, and Facebook Reels. TikTok is the highest-volume channel because its algorithm favors content discovery over follower count, which aligns perfectly with the Canvas UGC model." },
          { q: "How is Canvas UGC different from influencer marketing?", a: "In influencer marketing, the value is the creator's audience — they post on their own account and their followers see it. In Canvas UGC, creators post on a brand's account. The creator's personal audience size doesn't matter. The brand retains the content, the account growth, and all engagement data." },
          { q: "Can OKAD help me start a Canvas UGC program?", a: "Yes. We handle the entire operation — account setup, warmup, creator recruitment from our 600+ creator network, content management, cross-platform view tracking, and automated payouts. Email olga@okad.agency or book a call to discuss your goals." },
